<!DOCTYPE qhelp PUBLIC
  "-//Semmle//qhelp//EN"
  "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
<overview>
<p>
Attributes such as <code>cmakeFlags</code>, <code>mesonFlags</code>,
<code>configureFlags</code>, and <code>makeFlags</code> are lists of shell
argv elements. nixpkgs expands these lists through Bash, so a single string
literal that contains embedded whitespace is split into multiple arguments.
That silently changes the invoked command line and often breaks the build.
</p>
<p>
This is the same bug class reported by <code>nixpkgs-hammering</code>'s
<code>no-flags-spaces</code> lint.
</p>
</overview>

<recommendation>
<p>
Put each flag in its own list element. For example, write
<code>[ "-DFOO=bar" "-DBAZ=qux" ]</code> instead of
<code>[ "-DFOO=bar -DBAZ=qux" ]</code>.
</p>
</recommendation>

<example>
<p>Unsafe — one list element contains two shell words:</p>
<sample language="nix">
cmakeFlags = [ "-DFOO=bar baz" ];
</sample>
<p>Safe — each flag is a separate list element:</p>
<sample language="nix">
cmakeFlags = [ "-DFOO=bar" "-DBAZ=qux" ];
</sample>
</example>

<references>
<li>
CWE: <a href="https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html">CWE-78:
Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command</a>
</li>
</references>
</qhelp>
